<title>HUNGARY: Human boosts 1996 net profit to 712.1 mln.</title>
<headline>Human boosts 1996 net profit to 712.1 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		  653.4     vs     519.8</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		    712.5     vs     496.1</p>
<p>    After-tax profit		  712.1     vs     469.3</p>
<p>    Net sales revenue	    13,637.1     vs  10,412.4</p>
<p>    Other revenue		     165.0     vs     217.8</p>
<p>    Direct costs of sales	 9,910.2     vs   7,228.3</p>
<p>    Indirect costs of sales     2,766.0     vs   2,174.1</p>
<p>    Other expenditures		472.6     vs     685.9</p>
<p>    Net financial income	     67.9 profit vs    0.2 loss</p>
<p>     Financial revenue		125.0     vs	86.1</p>
<p>     Financial expenditure	   57.1     vs	86.3</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary income	  8.7 loss vs     23.5 loss</p>
<p>    Taxation				0.4     vs	26.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Human Rt is a pharmaceuticals company. The figures were calculated according to Hungarian Accounting Standards, they are consolidated. The 1996 figures are not yet audited.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
